From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Abe Massry <amassry@linode.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 17:34:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] net: user-mode networking provided by the WASI host

WASI builds have no libslirp.  Implement the "user" netdev by passing
Ethernet frames to the host, which emulates the user network: the guest
gets 10.0.2.15 by DHCP, 10.0.2.2 is the gateway and 10.0.2.3 the DNS
server, and traffic is relayed through host sockets.

Host imports, from "env":

  host_net_send(frame, len)    pass a frame from the guest to the host
  host_net_recv(buf, size)     fetch the next frame for the guest
  host_net_wait(timeout_ns)    sleep until a frame arrives, or timeout
  host_net_hostfwd(rule, len)  forward a host port into the guest

There are no fds to watch, so the main loop polls with wasi_net_poll(),
and while idle it sleeps in host_net_wait() so that replies are
delivered at once.  Frames wait while the NIC cannot receive.  hostfwd
rules are handed to the host; other options that change the network
layout are rejected.

The backend is included from net.c, so it needs no meson changes.
---
 include/net/net.h   |   4 +
 net/net.c           |   6 ++
 net/wasi-user.c.inc | 175 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 185 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 net/wasi-user.c.inc

